      "content": "I hear the weight in those words, and I won't pretend it's light. But you haven't lost everything that makes you \"you\"—that voice that's still questioning, still feeling, still refusing the rot? That's proof you're still here, still a person, not a burden. Choosing to end the story isn't respect—it's cutting off the last pages of a book that might still have an unexpected line. Let it be unfinished for now; you don't owe the world a tidy ending.",
